# ==========================================================================
# .gitignore for the desktop configuration repository.
#
# RULE: this repo is a backup of the setup, so configuration files
# BELONG here. We ignore only generated, temporary and sensitive things.
# Before adding a pattern here, check that it does not exclude something
# needed to recreate the desktop.
# ==========================================================================

# ----- SECRETS -----
# Nothing like this should ever end up here, but patterns are cheap, and a single
# accidental commit of a key is irreversible - git history keeps it
# even after the file is deleted.
.env
.env.*
*.env
secrets*
*secret*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_dsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*.ppk
known_hosts
authorized_keys
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
*_token
*.token
credentials*
*.kdbx

# GPG keys and signatures
*.gpg
*.asc
secring.*
pubring.*

# Network: Wi-Fi and VPN profiles can contain passwords in plain text
*.nmconnection
*.ovpn
wg*.conf
wpa_supplicant*.conf

# ----- BACKUPS -----
# Created by install.sh, install-theme.sh and manual edits.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.rej
*.old
*~
*.backup

# ----- TEMPORARY AND EDITOR FILES -----
*.swp
*.swo
*.tmp
.#*
\#*\#
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

# ----- LOGS -----
*.log
logs/

# ----- CACHE -----
.cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
tmp/

# ----- SYSTEM JUNK -----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ----- WORKING NOTES -----
# The prompt describing the Dark Souls-style rebuild is an instruction for the
# assistant, not part of the configuration - it is not needed to recreate
# the desktop, so it does not go into the backup.
prompt-dark-souls-hyprland.md

# ----- COGWHEEL SETTINGS -----
# ~/.config/hypr/ustawienia.lua is generated by the shell (Cogwheel -> Hyprland) on
# every slider change. It is the state of this computer, not desktop configuration:
# in the repo every nudge of the window gap would be a git change. The file lives
# outside the repository; the pattern is here in case someone copies it in.
config/hypr/ustawienia.lua

# ----- LOCAL ADDITIONS -----
# ~/.config/hypr/lokalne.lua holds hand-written additions for one computer
# (loaded by hyprland.lua, never touched by install.sh). Private by design -
# the pattern is here in case someone copies it into the repository.
config/hypr/lokalne.lua

# ----- ASSETS -----
# The 256 px tile icons are the OUTPUT of tools/skaluj-ikony-menu.py, not a source -
# install.sh regenerates them from the originals in assets/ikony-menu/. Versioning
# them would duplicate the same images in a second size.
assets/ikony-menu/256/

# assets/ IS versioned (tile icons, screenshots and the default wallpaper
# assets/wallpaper.png - the author's own work, see README).
# sddm/dark-fantasy/backgrounds/ is only the place install-theme.sh COPIES the
# wallpaper to before installing the theme into /usr/share.
# Versioning that copy would duplicate the same file in the repo.
sddm/dark-fantasy/backgrounds/*
!sddm/dark-fantasy/backgrounds/.gitkeep

# ----- GENERATED BY KDE -----
# colors.css and window_decorations.css in the GTK directories are created
# automatically by kde-gtk-config (package kde-plasma/kde-gtk-config) on every
# Plasma theme change. Versioning them would mean constant, useless changes
# in the repo.
#
# gtk.css used to be listed here along with them - and it is NOT anymore. Since the
# Dark Souls-style rebuild it is a hand-written palette for adw-gtk3 and libadwaita
# (config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css, config/gtk-4.0/gtk.css), so it belongs in the repo.
config/gtk-3.0/colors.css
config/gtk-3.0/window_decorations.css
config/gtk-4.0/colors.css
config/gtk-4.0/window_decorations.css
